CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1790107426
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G4/17
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3, V -,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, The IRA has claimed responsibility for
OL,6,Gthe blast at a Royal Marines barracks
OL,7, at Deal, Kent, today.
OL,8,F
OL,9,FOf the 10 people who were killed in the
OL,10,Fblast, nine were Royal Marine band
OL,11,Fmembers.
OL,12,F
OL,13,FDefence Secretary Mr Tom King visited
OL,14,Fthe wrecked building today and accused
OL,15,FIRA "godfathers" of an "appalling
OL,16,Foutrage against young army bandsmen".
OL,17,F
OL,18,FThe explosion occurred near a crowded
OL,19,Fstaff room as the musicians took a
OL,20,Fcoffee break before beginning the first
OL,21,Fpractice session of the day.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 22-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11805
SC,0005
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1790107426
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G5/17
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3, V -,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,4,F
OL,5, The Queen has sent a message to the
OL,6, Commandant General of the Royal Marines
OL,7, saying she is "deeply shocked" at the
OL,8, news of today's explosion in Kent.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThe Prime Minister, who is on her way
OL,11,Fto Moscow after a visit to Japan, said
OL,12,Fshe was "shocked and extremely sad".
OL,14,FShe expressed her condolences to the
OL,15,Frelatives of those killed at the Marine
OL,16,Fbarracks in Deal, and concern for the
OL,17,Fvictims.
OL,19,FIrish Prime Minister Mr Charles Haughey
OL,20,Fspoke of his horror and disgust at the
OL,21,Fblast.
OL,22,F
OL,23,T]CFrom 22-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11806
SC,0006
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1790107426
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G6/17
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3, V -,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,4,G
OL,5,GSeveral police files containing the
OL,6,Gphotographs of sixty terrorist suspects
OL,7,Ghave been delivered to the Belfast
OL,8,Goffice of the Independent newspaper.
OL,10,FThe files were headed RUC Criminal
OL,11,FIntelligence Section. They were later
OL,12,Fhanded to the detectives investigating
OL,13,Falleged collusion between the security
OL,14,Fforces and loyalist paramilitaries.
OL,16,FTwenty-five people in the latest batch
OL,17,Fcome from the Irish Republic. The BBC
OL,18,FNorthern Ireland Correspondent says
OL,19,Fthere may be suspicion these pictures
OL,20,Foriginated with police in the Republic.
OL,21,F
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]CFrom 22-09-89   teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
FL,119,180,120,250,0,100
PN,11807
SC,0007
CT,25,T
PS,c008
OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 2   F118A1790107426
OL,1,  V<,,4<,,4<,,4Spp0pp0p``0pp0      G7/17
OL,2,T]V5b(55b(55j5Sj5.%jj5/l4
OL,3, V -,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5,GThe Arab League's peace envoy in
OL,6,GLebanon has announced that Christian
OL,7,Gleader General Aoun has accepted the
OL,8,GLeague's peace plan.
OL,9,F
OL,10,FThe envoy, Mr Lakhdar Ibrahimi, made
OL,11,Fhis announcement after meeting the
OL,12,Fgeneral in a bunker below the ruined
OL,13,Fpresidential palace in east Beirut.
OL,14,F
OL,15,FMr Ibrahimi said he hoped to form a
OL,16,Fcommittee to implement the plan which
OL,17,Fcould have its first meeting tomorrow.
OL,18,F
OL,19,S/FThree people were killed and 16
OL,20,Finjured overnight in four hours of
OL,21,Fheavy shelling in the east.
OL,22,F
OL,23,D]CFrom 22-09-89   teletextarchive.com
